.TH DVBTX-WEB 7 2026-11-08 "dvbtx 0.3.0" "dvbtx manual"
.SH NAME
dvbtx-web \- the dvbtx monitoring and control web page and its HTTP API
.SH DESCRIPTION
While
.BR dvbtx (1)
runs, it serves a single web page and a JSON API over plain HTTP.
The page shows the radios, the multiplexes, every channel and every source with
statistics refreshed each second, and lets the operator stop or start a multiplex,
add, edit or remove channels, restart a source, edit the configuration file and
apply it, save and load profiles, and watch a channel live.
The same operations are available to programs through the HTTP API described
below; the
.B dvbtx channel
commands of
.BR dvbtx\-channel (1)
use it.
.PP
The page itself is in French; this manual describes it in English and quotes
its labels as they appear on screen.
.SH REACHING THE PAGE
The server is started by the supervisor before the sources, so the page is up
while the sources are still being resolved.
It listens on
.B web.listen
of the configuration file, by default
.BR 127.0.0.1:8080 ,
that is
.UR http://127.0.0.1:8080/
.UE
on the transmitter only.
To reach it from the local network, listen on every address:
.PP
.EX
[web]
listen = "0.0.0.0:8080"
.EE
.PP
or on the command line
.B \-\-web 0.0.0.0:8080
(or
.BR "\-s web.listen=0.0.0.0:8080" ).
A
.B listen
with an empty host (\(lq:8080\(rq) also binds every address.
.B \-\-web none
or
.B web.enabled = false
runs without the page.
If the address cannot be bound, dvbtx logs the error and runs without it.
.PP
The page is meant for a trusted LAN.
Nothing is ever asked to read it: the page, the statistics, the previews and
.B /metrics
are open to whoever reaches the port.
The requests that change something (POST, PATCH, DELETE) are guarded as follows:
.TP
.B Cross\-site refusal
A request carrying an
.B Origin
header whose host and port differ from its
.B Host
header is refused with status 403
("request from another web site refused"):
a page of another web site cannot drive the transmitter through the browser of
someone who has the page open.
Programs such as
.BR curl (1)
send no
.B Origin
and are accepted.
.TP
.B JSON body
The requests that carry a body must have
.BR "Content\-Type: application/json" ,
else status 415.
The body must be a JSON object of at most 65536 bytes, else status 400.
.TP
.B Token
When
.B web.token
is set (empty by default), every change must carry it, as
.B Authorization: Bearer
.I token
or as
.B X\-Dvbtx\-Token:
.IR token ,
else status 401 ("token required (web.token)").
On a 401 the page asks for the token once (\(lqJeton de l'émetteur (web.token) :\(rq),
keeps it in the browser's local storage and repeats the request.
.TP
.B Exec sources
Sources that run a command or read standard input
.RB ( exec: ,
.BR pipe: ,
.BR stdin: ,
.BR \- )
and the options that pass raw arguments to ffmpeg
.RB ( ffmpeg_input ,
.BR ffmpeg_output )
are refused from the API unless
.B web.allow_exec_sources = true
(default false); the configuration file may always use them.
.SH THE PAGE
The page polls
.B /api/status
every second,
.B /api/history
every 2 s and
.B /api/config
every 10 s.
.SS Header and banners
The header shows the network name (the
.B [network]
name, also the browser tab title), a pill for the engine
(\(lqmoteur actif\(rq, \(lqmoteur arrêté\(rq, or \(lqdvbtx injoignable\(rq when the page
cannot reach dvbtx), the number of active alerts (\(lqaucune alerte\(rq when none),
the dvbtx version, the uptime, and \(lqstats vieilles de
.I N
s\(rq when the engine statistics are more than 5 s old.
.PP
Below the header, on every tab:
.IP \(bu 2
the active alerts, one line each, with their level
(\(lqCritique\(rq, \(lqAttention\(rq, \(lqInfo\(rq), message and age;
.IP \(bu
a red banner when the configuration file as saved is not valid;
.IP \(bu
the
.B pending changes
banner (\(lqModifications enregistrées, pas encore appliquées\(rq), listing what
differs between the file and what runs, with the buttons
\(lqAnnuler les modifications\(rq and \(lqAppliquer\(rq; see
.B Pending changes and Apply
below.
.SS Tabs and anchors
Five tabs, each with an anchor that can be put in the address:
.TP
.B #etat
\(lqTableau de bord\(rq, the dashboard (radios, machine load, multiplexes).
.TP
.B #chaines
\(lqChaînes\(rq, the channels of each multiplex.
.TP
.B #sources
\(lqSources\(rq, the ingest processes and GPU transcoding.
.TP
.B #config
\(lqConfiguration\(rq, the configuration file: network, radios, multiplexes,
profiles, bit rate calculator.
Its tab label carries the number of pending changes.
.TP
.B #journaux
\(lqJournaux\(rq, the engine log and the alert history.
.PP
With no anchor, the browser opens the tab it showed last (kept in its local storage),
else the dashboard.
Two more parameters can follow the tab, separated by
.BR & ,
and act once, when the page loads:
.TP
.BI live= sid
opens the live view of the channel whose service_id is
.I sid
(decimal), e.g.
.BR #chaines&live=257 .
.TP
.BI detail= sid
opens the detail window of that channel, e.g.
.BR #chaines&detail=257 .
.SS Dashboard: radios
One card per radio that carries at least one multiplex: name, driver, LO
frequency, sample rate, gain (\(lq+ ampli\(rq when the HackRF amplifier is on),
buffer fill (\(lqTampon\(rq, in %), CPU of its synthesis and USB thread
(\(lqCPU (synthèse + USB)\(rq, in % of one core) with a sparkline of it.
CPU figures of radios, multiplexes and sources are in % of one core (100 % is one
whole core); the Machine gauge is in % of all the cores.
.PP
The state pill reflects the radio state reported by the engine:
.TP
.B on
on the air: \(lq0 sous\-débit\(rq, or the number of underruns in red
(\(lq\fIN\fP sous\-débits\(rq).
.TP
.B idle
switched off on purpose, all its multiplexes being stopped:
\(lqéteinte \(bu ses multiplex sont arrêtés\(rq.
.TP
.B off
not found at the start: \(lqintrouvable \(bu ses multiplex sont coupés\(rq.
.TP
.B lost
lost while on the air (unplugged, USB error): \(lqperdue \(bu ses multiplex sont coupés\(rq.
.PP
For
.B off
and
.BR lost ,
the driver's error follows, with \(lqrecherchée toutes les 15 s\(rq: the radio
is probed every 15 s and the engine is started again once it is back (a short cut
of the other radios); a radio lost for 120 s and not found again also restarts the
engine.
Only the multiplexes of that radio are off the air, their sources paused; the
other radios go on.
.PP
An edgeQAM board (driver
.BR edgeqam ,
.BR dvbtx.toml (5))
has its own card: \(lqen lien\(rq while it answers, \(lqla carte ne répond pas\(rq in red when it
does not, its address and the frequency of its multiplex 1, and one row per multiplex: the state of its
buffer (\(lqsuivi\(rq: tracked, \(lqremplissage\(rq: being filled, \(lqvidage\(rq: being drained),
the packets waiting in it, the rate trim in ppm and, when there are some, the nulls the board
inserted and the packets it dropped since it started.
.SS Dashboard: machine
Half\-circle gauges: \(lqCPU\(rq for the whole machine (all processes, with the
number of cores), and one \(lqGPU\(rq gauge per graphics adapter with its two
busiest engines (render, video, encoder...).
.SS Dashboard: multiplexes
One card per multiplex.
Its header line, shown on both the dashboard and the channels tab, has:
.IP \(bu 2
the name, an \(lqarrêté\(rq pill when the multiplex is stopped, the standard and
its parameters, the frequency, the TSID and the radio;
.IP \(bu
\(lqcapacité\(rq, the useful bit rate of the channel in Mbit/s, and
\(lqoccupé\(rq, the occupancy: useful (non\-null) bit rate averaged over 10 s
divided by the capacity, orange above 90 %, red above 98 %;
.IP \(bu
\(lqmodulation\(rq, the CPU of this multiplex's modulation thread;
\(lqsources\(rq, the CPU of the ffmpeg processes of its channels; and
\(lqGPU\(rq, the GPU load of its re\-encoded channels (details on hover);
.IP \(bu
the
.B \(lqArrêter\(rq / \(lqDémarrer\(rq
button (see
.B Stopping and starting a multiplex
below);
.IP \(bu
a bar of the capacity split between the channels, the PSI/SI tables and the free
part (\(lqlibre\(rq), each averaged over the last 10 s, with its legend.
.PP
The dashboard card adds a graph of the useful bit rate over the last 10 minutes
against the capacity (dashed line), the address of the multiplex's UDP copy
(\(lqcopie du TS\(rq,
.BI udp://127.0.0.1: port
with
.I port
= ingest.monitor_base_port + index, 20900 by default), the
.B TS
link (see
.BR Previews ),
and, when TSDuck analyses the multiplex, its bit rate, transport errors,
discontinuities, the age of the report and a \(lqrapport complet\(rq link to
.BR /api/analysis/\fIn\fP .
.SS Stopping and starting a multiplex
The button \(lqArrêter\(rq of a multiplex (after a confirmation:
\(lqArrêter l'émission de ce multiplex ? Les autres continuent.\(rq) sends
.BR "POST /api/carrier/\fIn\fP/stop" ;
\(lqDémarrer\(rq sends
.BR "POST /api/carrier/\fIn\fP/start" ,
without confirmation.
.PP
A stopped multiplex goes off the air at once; the other multiplexes, on the same
radio or not, are not interrupted.
The primary sources of its channels are paused (their ffmpeg stopped) and come
back when it is started again.
A radio whose multiplexes are all stopped is switched off (state
.BR idle )
and switched on again with the first one started.
No alert is raised for a stopped multiplex.
.PP
The state is written to the configuration file at once
.RB ( "enabled = false"
in its
.B [[carrier]]
table, removed when started again) and is kept across restarts.
It is not a pending change: it applies immediately and needs no \(lqAppliquer\(rq.
.SS Channels tab
The button \(lqRecharger EPG / SI\(rq re\-reads the programme guide from the EPG
folder and URLs and rebuilds the SI tables
.RB ( "POST /api/reload" ).
.PP
Each multiplex has the header line described above, the button
\(lq+ Ajouter une chaîne\(rq and a table of its channels, one row each:
.TP
.B LCN
the logical channel number.
.TP
.B Chaîne
a colour mark (the colour of the occupancy bar), the name, the service_id in
hexadecimal, the service type and the priority; for a re\-encoded channel,
\(lqréencodée, cible
.I X
Mbit/s (poids
.IR W )\(rq,
its target video bit rate and bit rate weight.
.TP
.B Source
the source on air: \(lqprincipale\(rq (primary, green), \(lqsecours\(rq (the
backup clip, orange) or \(lqaucune\(rq (none, red).
With several sources, \(lqsource
.IR k / n \(rq
tells which one plays, and \(lqessai de la
.IR j \(rq
when a preferred one is being tried beside it.
.TP
.B "Entrée Mbit/s, Sortie Mbit/s"
the bit rate received from the source and the bit rate sent in the multiplex.
.TP
.B Marge vidéo
the
.B decoding margin
of the video: for each frame, the time between its emission and its decoding
time in the receiver (DTS minus the PCR at emission), the minimum over the last
second, with the mean below (\(lqmoy\(rq).
About 700 ms normally; lower when the multiplex is too full; below zero the TV
freezes.
Green, orange below
.B alerts.margin_min_ms
(150 ms by default), red below zero.
A sparkline column (\(lq10 min\(rq) follows, with the alert threshold dashed.
.TP
.B Marge audio
the same for the audio.
.TP
.B Retard ms
the gap between the sending of the packets and their ideal time, the worst of each
second: negative is early (normal, up to the service's
.BR early_ms ,
100 ms by default), positive is late, shown bold; beyond
.B max_late_ms
(600 ms by default) packets are dropped, shown as \(lq\fIN\fP perdus\(rq.
.TP
.B Pertes entrée
continuity errors in the stream received from the source since its input
started: packets lost between the source and dvbtx.
.TP
.B Aperçu
the thumbnail of the channel (see
.BR Previews );
a click on it opens the live view.
The eye in the column header hides or shows the thumbnails.
.TP
.B En cours
now and next from the EPG (\(lqpas d'EPG\(rq when there is none).
.TP
.I last column
an information icon opening the detail window, a pencil icon opening the edit
dialog, and a red cross removing the channel (after a confirmation).
.PP
When a multiplex is full, the channels of lower priority take the delay, then the
losses, first.
.SS Channel detail window
Opened by the information icon or
.BR #detail=\fIsid\fP ,
it charts one channel over a period of \(lq15 min\(rq, \(lq1 h\(rq (default),
\(lq6 h\(rq or \(lq24 h\(rq, from
.BR /api/channel/\fIsid\fP/rates :
.IP \(bu 2
\(lqDébit\(rq: the output bit rate, mean of each time slice with a band from its
minimum to its maximum, the 95th percentile dashed, and a table of mean, minimum,
median, 95th percentile and maximum;
.IP \(bu
\(lqRetard d'envoi\(rq: the lateness, worst of each slice;
.IP \(bu
\(lqMarge vidéo\(rq: the video decoding margin, lowest of each slice, with its
minimum, 5th percentile and median, and the alert threshold dashed;
.IP \(bu
\(lqPertes en entrée\(rq: input continuity errors counted per slice, or
\(lqaucune sur la période\(rq.
.PP
The measures are taken once a second and kept 24 hours in memory; they are lost
when dvbtx restarts.
.SS Adding, editing and removing a channel
\(lq+ Ajouter une chaîne\(rq and the pencil icon open the same dialog
(\(lqAjouter une chaîne\(rq or \(lqModifier
.IR name \(rq):
.TP
.B Multiplex
the multiplex of the new channel (shown when adding, with more than one
multiplex).
.TP
.B Nom
the name, 1 to 60 characters, no quotes or backslashes.
.TP
.B Numéro (LCN)
1 to 1023; empty when adding: the first free number.
When editing, the box \(lqsi le numéro est pris, échanger avec cette chaîne\(rq
swaps the numbers with the channel that had it; without it, a number in use is
refused.
.TP
.B Sources
one source per line, in order of preference: when the one playing fails, the
next takes over, and the channel comes back to a preferred one once it works
again; all down: the backup clip.
A change of source does not cut the channel.
See
.BR dvbtx\-sources (7).
.TP
.B Cache (ms)
.BR buffer_ms ,
100 to 30000; empty is
.B auto
(6000 for YouTube, Twitch and HLS, 1000 otherwise; the value in use is shown as
the placeholder).
.TP
.B Vidéo de secours
the backup clip; empty: none.
A new channel is prefilled with the default backup.
.TP
.B Priorité
1 to 10, 5 being normal (\(lqnormale\(rq); 1 loses first (\(lqperdue en premier\(rq),
10 last (\(lqperdue en dernier\(rq).
.TP
.B Part du débit (si réencodée)
the
.B bitrate_weight
of a re\-encoded channel: \(lqSD (1)\(rq, \(lqHD 720p (2)\(rq, \(lqFull HD (3)\(rq,
\(lq4K (6)\(rq.
A re\-encoded channel takes a share of what the copied channels leave, according
to its weight; a copied channel keeps its source's bit rate and only the
priority matters for it.
.TP
.B Débit vidéo max (Mbit/s)
the
.B max_bitrate
of a re\-encoded channel, 0.5 to 80; empty: the default (8 Mbit/s,
.BR defaults.encode.max_auto_bitrate ).
.PP
\(lqEnregistrer\(rq saves, \(lqAnnuler\(rq closes.
Removing a channel asks \(lqSupprimer la chaîne ... ? Les autres chaînes ne sont pas
touchées.\(rq
.PP
From the page, adding, editing and removing a channel are
.B pending changes:
the page sends its requests with
.BR ?apply=0 ,
which only writes the configuration file; nothing changes on air until
\(lqAppliquer\(rq.
From the API without
.BR ?apply=0 ,
as
.BR dvbtx\-channel (1)
does, the change is applied at once to that channel only and written to the file.
.SS Sources tab
One row per ingest process (the primary sources, the backup clips, and the
sources being tried or held in standby beside a channel):
.TP
.B #
the input index, used by
.BR /api/input/\fIn\fP/restart .
.TP
.B Source
the channel name (\(lq(secours)\(rq for a backup clip) and the source.
.TP
.B État
the process state:
.BR running ,
.BR restarting ,
.BR backoff ,
.BR paused ,
.BR stopped ,
.BR error ,
or \(lqUDP direct\(rq for a source read by the engine without ffmpeg; the last
error below.
.TP
.B Traitement
what ffmpeg does: \(lqcopie\(rq (copy), \(lqcopie vidéo\(rq with the audio
re\-encoded, \(lqCPU\(rq or \(lqGPU\(rq transcoding with the codec (and the
adapter for the GPU).
.TP
.B Img/s \(bu vitesse
frames per second of a transcode, and the speed against real time, in red when
below 0.97 after 20 s.
.TP
.B Perdues
frames dropped / duplicated by ffmpeg.
.TP
.B "CPU, GPU"
the CPU of the source's processes (% of one core) and its busiest GPU engine.
.TP
.B "Relances, Débit, Inactif"
the number of restarts, the bit rate received, and the time since the last
packet.
.TP
.B Journal
a button with the number of log lines; it opens, under the row, the ffmpeg
command and its last 50 lines.
.TP
.B Relancer
(ffmpeg sources only) restarts the process
.RB ( "POST /api/input/\fIn\fP/restart" ).
.PP
Below, \(lqTranscodage : GPU\(rq shows the GPU manager: its state
(\(lqdésactivé (ingest.gpu)\(rq, \(lqaucune carte utilisable\(rq, \(lqprêt\(rq,
\(lqapprentissage en cours\(rq, \(lqéchec de l'apprentissage\(rq), the progress
of a learning and its date, and for each adapter its driver, the number of
transcodes it runs, or why it is not usable, and for H.264, HEVC and MPEG\-2 the
best way learnt (frames per second, CPU per frame) or \(lqnon\(rq with the
reason.
The button \(lqRéapprendre les GPU\(rq
.RB ( "POST /api/gpu/learn" )
runs the learning again in the background, the CPU transcoding meanwhile; it is
absent when GPU transcoding is off or no adapter is usable, and disabled while a
learning runs.
.SS Previews
Every preview reads a copy of what goes on air, asked to the engine for the time
of the preview, so it shows what the TVs receive, backup clip included.
Nothing runs while nobody looks.
.TP
.B Thumbnails
Shown by default
.RB ( web.preview_thumbnails ,
true); the eye of the \(lqAperçu\(rq column hides or shows them, and the browser
remembers that choice.
They are requested only while the channels tab is visible.
For each multiplex, one ffmpeg reads the multiplex just long enough to write
one 320 pixel wide JPEG of a key frame per channel with a picture, then stops;
the next shot comes
.B web.preview_thumb_every_s
later (60 s by default, 2 s at least).
Key frames are decoded on the GPU when the transcodes have one.
A multiplex's thumbnails stop 60 s after the last request for them.
.TP
.B Live view
A click on a thumbnail, or
.BR #live=\fIsid\fP ,
opens the \(lqDirect\(rq window: the channel as on air, a few seconds late.
H.264 video is copied, only the container (MPEG\-TS to fragmented MP4) and the
sound (to AAC, 96 kbit/s stereo) change; other video codecs are re\-encoded to
360 lines (libx264, 900 kbit/s).
The box \(lqréencoder (si l'image ne s'affiche pas)\(rq forces the re\-encoding.
The window links to the multiplex's TS.
Closing it stops the ffmpeg.
.TP
.B TS link
\(lqTS\(rq on each multiplex card (and \(lqTS du multiplex\(rq in the live window)
is the multiplex exactly as it goes on air, every channel, relayed without ffmpeg
.RB ( /api/mux/\fIn\fP.ts ),
for mpv, VLC, ffplay...
.PP
Live views and TS streams together are limited to
.B web.preview_max_live
(4 by default); one more is answered with status 503.
Thumbnails do not count.
.SS Configuration tab
The configuration tab edits the configuration file
.BR dvbtx.toml (5).
It needs one: with channels given on the command line it shows
\(lqno configuration file\(rq and the dialogs refuse to open.
.PP
Every change is checked (the whole file must still build, as at start\-up) and
written to the file at once, its comments and layout kept.
Nothing changes on air until it is applied.
.TP
.B Réseau
\(lqNom du réseau\(rq, \(lqFournisseur\(rq, \(lqONID (original_network_id)\(rq,
\(lqnetwork_id\(rq, \(lqCode pays (ISO 3166, 3 lettres)\(rq,
\(lqFuseau horaire\(rq, saved by \(lqEnregistrer\(rq
.RB ( "PATCH /api/config/network" ).
The list \(lqPays (remplit ONID, réseau, code)\(rq fills the ONID and network_id with
0x2000 plus the ISO 3166 numeric code of the country (the terrestrial rule of
ETSI TS 101 162: France 250 gives 0x20FA, the default) and the country code.
Many TVs ignore the logical channel numbers of a network whose ONID is not
their country's.
ONID and network_id accept decimal or 0x hexadecimal, 0 to 0xFFFF.
An emptied field removes the key from the file (its default then applies).
.TP
.B Radios
a table (name, driver, gain, sample rate, arguments) with \(lqModifier\(rq on each
row and \(lq+ Ajouter une radio\(rq.
The dialog has \(lqNom\(rq, \(lqPilote\(rq (driver), \(lqNuméro de série\(rq
.RB ( serial :
the device the radio is bound to, empty: the first one of its driver),
\(lqenregistrer automatiquement le numéro de série d'une carte libre de ce pilote\(rq
(the devices of the driver are listed with
.BR /api/devices ;
the one no other radio is bound to fills the serial, a list offers them when there are several),
\(lqArguments\(rq,
\(lqGain (dB)\(rq, \(lqRecul (dB)\(rq
.RB ( backoff_db ),
\(lqÉchantillonnage (MS/s)\(rq
.RB ( rate ),
\(lqLO (MHz)\(rq
.RB ( center ),
\(lqDécalage du LO\(rq
.RB ( lo_offset )
and \(lqamplificateur RF (HackRF)\(rq
.RB ( amp );
an empty field is automatic.
For an
.B edgeqam
board the radio fields give way to \(lqAdresse de la carte\(rq
.RB ( address ,
empty: found by mDNS) and \(lqrégler sa fréquence et couper ses multiplex inutilisés\(rq
.RB ( tune ).
\(lqSupprimer\(rq removes the radio, refused while a multiplex uses it.
Renaming a radio renames it in the multiplexes that name it.
.TP
.B Multiplex
a table (name, radio, standard, frequency, modulation, capacity, number of
channels) with \(lqModifier\(rq and \(lq+ Ajouter un multiplex\(rq.
The dialog has \(lqNom\(rq, \(lqRadio\(rq, \(lqNorme\(rq (DVB\-T, DVB\-T2,
DVB\-C, DVB\-S, DVB\-S2; DVB\-T2 for a new one), \(lqFréquence (MHz)\(rq,
\(lqTSID\(rq (empty: automatic) and the parameters of the standard, with the
useful bit rate (\(lqdébit utile\(rq) and the rate per channel computed as
they change.
A change of standard drops the parameters of the old one; setting a frequency
drops a
.B channel
key.
\(lqSupprimer\(rq removes the multiplex with all its channels.
.TP
.B Profils
see
.B Profiles
below.
.TP
.B Calculateur de débit utile
the useful bit rate of a channel for a standard and its parameters, and the
rate per channel for a number of channels (\(lqChaînes\(rq), 3 % being kept for
the tables
.RB ( /api/calc ).
.SS Pending changes and Apply
The file as saved is compared with the configuration running; the differences
are the pending changes, listed in the banner (radio, multiplex, channel or
settings section added, removed, or changed with the old and new value of each
key) and counted on the configuration tab.
.TP
.B Appliquer
.RB ( "POST /api/config/apply" )
applies the file.
When only channels changed (or the
.B [defaults]
or
.B [power]
tables), they are applied one by one and the other channels are not cut
(\(lqSeules les chaînes changent : les autres ne sont pas coupées.\(rq).
Any other change (radios, multiplexes, network or other settings) restarts the
transmission, a few seconds without signal; the page asks for a confirmation
first, the unchanged sources keep running, and TVs may need a new scan.
If the engine refuses the new configuration (it stops before its first statistics), the
previous one is put back on the air, the page shows the engine's error, and the changes stay
pending in the file, to correct or cancel.
A radio left without multiplex is not given to the engine.
.TP
.B Annuler les modifications
.RB ( "POST /api/config/revert" ,
after a confirmation) writes the configuration running back over the file.
It is refused when radios or multiplexes were added or removed, or a section
changed in sub\-tables: load a profile, or edit them back.
.PP
The \(lqArrêter\(rq / \(lqDémarrer\(rq buttons of the multiplexes are not
pending changes (see above).
.SS Profiles
Profiles are copies of the configuration file beside it,
.IB file . name
(for example
.BR /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml.night ),
a name being 1 to 40 letters, digits, \- or _, other than
.B bak
and
.BR tmp .
The \(lqProfils\(rq section lists them with their date, \(lq= fichier actuel\(rq
when one is identical to the file, and the buttons:
.TP
.B Enregistrer la configuration actuelle comme profil
copies the file (as saved, pending changes included) to the profile named in the
field beside it.
.TP
.B Charger
checks the profile, keeps the current file as
.IB file .bak
and copies the profile over the file; the result is pending until
\(lqAppliquer\(rq.
.TP
.B \(lq\(mu\(rq (red cross)
deletes the profile.
.PP
Only the file itself is ever applied.
.SH HTTP API
All answers are JSON unless stated otherwise, with
.BR "Cache\-Control: no\-store" .
Statuses: 200 done, 204 no picture yet, 400 invalid or refused
(\fB{"ok":false,"error":\fP ...\fB}\fP),
401 token missing, 403 cross\-site request, 404 unknown route or object,
415 body not JSON, 503 too many live previews.
.PP
In the paths,
.I n
is the index of a multiplex (0 for the first), or of an input for
.BR /api/input ;
.I sid
is a service_id in decimal;
.I i
is the position of a
.B [[radio]]
or
.B [[carrier]]
table in the file, from 0.
.I channel
designates a channel by its number (LCN), its service_id
.RB ( 0x0101
or
.BR sid:257 )
or its name (URL\-encoded, case ignored; an ambiguous name is refused).
.PP
Requests that change something answer
\fB{"ok":true,\fP ...\fB}\fP
with the fields of the change, or status 400 with
\fB{"ok":false,"error":\fP ...\fB}\fP.
They run in the supervisor's main loop; one that gets no answer in 120 s fails.
.SS Reading
.TP
\fBGET /\fR, \fBGET /index.html\fR
the page.
.TP
.B GET /api/status
everything the page shows; see
.B /api/status
below.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/history?last=" seconds
the short\-term series, one point per engine statistics line (each second), at most
1800 points; default
.BR last=600 .
Answer
\fB{"t":[\fItimes\fB],"series":{\fIkey\fB:[\fIvalues\fB]}}\fP,
keys
.BI c n .rate
(useful bit rate),
.BI c n .null ,
.BI c n .si ,
.BI c n .lead ,
.BI s n . sid .rate ,
.BI s n . sid .vmargin ,
.BI s n . sid .amargin ,
.BI s n . sid .late
and
.BI r n .cpu .
.TP
.BI "GET /api/channel/" sid /rates?hours= h
a channel over the last
.I h
hours (default 6, 0.05 to 24), in about 360 time slices.
Answer
\fB{"from", "to", "rate", "late", "margin", "cc"}\fP,
each measure being
\fB{"t", "mean", "min", "max", "sum", "stats"}\fP
(per slice) with
.B stats
= mean, min, max, median, p5, p95, total, samples;
.B cc
counts the continuity errors gained in each slice.
404 \(lqno data for this channel yet\(rq.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/analysis/" n
the last full TSDuck
.B analyze
JSON report of multiplex
.IR n ;
404 \(lqno report\(rq when TSDuck is off or has not reported yet.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/epg/" sid
the EPG events of a service (at most 200):
\fB[{"event_id", "start", "duration", "title", "subtitle"}]\fP.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/devices?driver=" d "\fR[\fP&radio=" i \fR]\fP
the devices of a driver plugged in, as
.BR hackrf_info ,
.B uhd_find_devices
or
.B SoapySDRUtil
see them (a few seconds), plus those the engine has open:
\fB{"driver", "devices": [{"serial", "label", "open", "radio"}], "free": [serial...], "error"}\fP.
.B radio
is the radio of the configuration file bound to the device (its
.BR serial ),
or the one holding it (a radio without serial opens the first device of its driver);
.B free
the devices with none.
.BI radio= i
leaves out radio
.I i
of the file (the one being edited: its own device is free for it).
.B error
says why nothing could be listed (tool missing, no answer).
The radio cards of the status show the serial of each radio as its driver reports it.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/calc?standard=" std & key = value ...
the useful bit rate of a channel:
.B standard
is
.BR dvbt " (default), " dvbt2 ", " dvbc ", " dvbs " or " dvbs2 ,
the other parameters those of
.BR dvbtx.toml (5)
.RB ( bandwidth
and
.B symbol_rate
in Hz or symbol/s;
.BR pilots ,
.B extended
and
.B rotation
as 1, true or on), plus
.B services
(default 1).
Answer
\fB{"rate", "per_service"}\fP,
.B per_service
being 97 % of the rate divided by the number of services; 400 with an error
for impossible parameters.
.TP
.B GET /api/channels
the channels:
\fB[{"carrier", "carrier_name", "lcn", "sid", "name", "source", "sources", "active", "backup", "pid_base", "visible", "provider", "on"}]\fP,
.B on
being the source on air
.RB ( primary ,
.BR backup ,
.BR none ,
or null).
.TP
.B GET /api/config
the configuration file:
.B path
(null without a file, with
.BR error ),
.B error
(why the file as saved is not valid, else null),
.BR drivers ,
.BR std_keys ,
.BR radio_defaults ,
.B network
(with its defaults),
.BR network_keys ,
.B radios
and
.B carriers
as written in the file (each multiplex with its number of
.B services
and its
.BR capacity ),
.B pending
(\fB[{"what":"radio|carrier|channel|settings", "op":"added|removed|changed", "name", "keys":{\fIkey\fB:[\fIold\fB,\fInew\fB]}}]\fP),
.B restart
(true when applying restarts the transmission) and
.B profiles
(\fB[{"name", "mtime", "same"}]\fP).
.TP
.B GET /api/gpu
the GPU manager:
\fB{"mode", "state", "progress", "learnt_at", "cache", "fingerprint", "devices"}\fP,
.B state
being
.BR off ,
.BR none ,
.BR ready ,
.B learning
or
.BR error ;
each device with its
.B load
(transcodes running) and the
.B results
of the learning per codec; or
\fB{"state":"off"}\fP
when there is no GPU manager.
.TP
.BI "GET /api/preview/" sid .jpg
the last thumbnail of a channel (image/jpeg), or status 204 with no body while
the first one is coming (also for an unknown channel).
Each request keeps the thumbnails of that multiplex going for 60 s.
.TP
\fBGET /api/preview/\fIsid\fB/live.mp4\fR[\fB?transcode=1\fR]
the channel live as fragmented MP4 (video/mp4), for as long as the connection
stays open;
.B transcode=1
re\-encodes the video even when it is H.264.
404 \(lqno such channel\(rq, 503 beyond
.BR web.preview_max_live .
.TP
.BI "GET /api/mux/" n .ts
multiplex
.I n
exactly as on air (video/mp2t), every channel, relayed from the engine's copy
for as long as it is read (the stream ends after 10 s without data).
404 \(lqno such multiplex\(rq, 503 beyond
.BR web.preview_max_live .
.TP
.BI "GET /api/mux/" n .m3u?program= sid
an M3U playlist (audio/x\-mpegurl) opening that stream, with
.BI #EXTVLCOPT:program= sid
so that VLC plays that channel.
The URL in it is built from the request's
.B Host
header.
.TP
.B GET /metrics
Prometheus exposition; see
.B /metrics
below.
.SS Actions
.TP
.BI "POST /api/carrier/" n /stop \fR,\fP " POST /api/carrier/" n /start
stops or starts multiplex
.IR n ;
no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"enabled":\fIbool\fB}\fP;
nothing is done when it already is in that state.
See
.B Stopping and starting a multiplex
above.
.TP
.BI "POST /api/input/" n /restart
restarts the ingest process of input
.IR n ;
no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true}\fP,
404 \(lqno such input\(rq.
.TP
.B POST /api/reload
re\-reads the EPG and rebuilds the SI tables; no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true}\fP.
.TP
.B POST /api/gpu/learn
learns the graphics adapters again, in the background; no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"started":\fIbool\fB}\fP,
.B started
false when a learning already runs; 400 when GPU transcoding is off
.RB ( ingest.gpu ).
.SS Channels
.TP
.B POST /api/channels
adds a channel.
Body:
.B name
and
.B source
(a string, or a list in order of preference) required;
.B carrier
(index or name, required when there are several multiplexes),
.B lcn
(default the first free),
.B sid
(number, or a string such as "0x0105"; default a free one),
.B backup
(a file, or false for none), and any service option of
.BR dvbtx.toml (5)
.RB ( priority ,
.BR bitrate_weight ,
.BR max_bitrate ,
.BR buffer_ms ,
\&...); null or empty values are ignored.
.TP
.BI "PATCH /api/channels/" channel
changes a channel.
Body: any of
.BR name ,
.B lcn
(with
\fB"swap":true\fP
to exchange numbers with the channel that has it),
.BR source ,
.B backup
("", false or null: none) and service options (null removes one).
.B sid
and
.B carrier
cannot be changed: remove the channel and add it again.
.TP
.BI "DELETE /api/channels/" channel
removes a channel; no body.
.PP
Without a query, the change is applied at once to that channel only (the others
lose no packet; a change of source switches on a key frame of the new one; a
change of an engine setting of the service, such as
.BR priority ,
re\-creates it, a brief cut of that channel) and
written to the configuration file, sid, lcn and pid_base being pinned so that
nothing shifts.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true, "sid", "changes":[\fItext\fB, ...], "detail":[{"what", "name", "from", "to"}], "saved", "applied", "warning"}\fP,
.B warning
saying why the file was not written.
.PP
With
.B ?apply=0
(what the page sends) the change is only written to the file, pending until
.BR "POST /api/config/apply" ;
answer
\fB{"ok":true, "saved":true, "pending":true, "sid"}\fP.
.SS Configuration file
These need a configuration file and only write it; the transmitter follows on
.BR "POST /api/config/apply" .
.TP
.BI "PATCH /api/config/radio/" i  \fR,\fP " PATCH /api/config/carrier/" i
changes keys of a
.B [[radio]]
or
.B [[carrier]]
table:
\fB{"\fIkey\fB":\fIvalue\fB, "\fIkey\fB":null}\fP,
null removing a key.
Unknown keys are refused.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"saved":true}\fP,
or
\fB{"ok":true,"saved":false,"unchanged":true}\fP
when nothing differs.
.TP
.B PATCH /api/config/network
changes
.BR name ,
.BR provider ,
.BR onid ,
.BR network_id ,
.B country
and
.B timezone
of
.B [network]
(null removes); other keys are refused.
Answer as above.
.TP
.BR "POST /api/config/radio" ", " "POST /api/config/carrier"
appends a radio or a multiplex:
\fB{"name":\fP ...\fB}\fP,
null values left out.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"saved":true}\fP.
.TP
.BI "DELETE /api/config/radio/" i  \fR,\fP " DELETE /api/config/carrier/" i
removes a radio (refused while a multiplex uses it) or a multiplex with its
channels.
.TP
.B POST /api/config/apply
applies the file; no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"restarted":true,"detail":[\fP...\fB]}\fP
when the transmission was restarted, else the answer of a channel change with
\fB"restarted":false\fP
and
.B detail
listing the pending changes applied.
.TP
.B POST /api/config/revert
the file back to the configuration running; no body.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"saved":\fIbool\fB}\fP.
.TP
.B POST /api/profiles
saves the file as profile
\fB{"name":"\fIname\fB"}\fP.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"saved":true,"profile":"\fIname\fB"}\fP.
.TP
.BI "POST /api/profiles/" name /load
copies a profile over the file (the old file kept as
.IR file .bak);
pending until applied.
.TP
.BI "DELETE /api/profiles/" name
deletes a profile.
Answer
\fB{"ok":true,"deleted":true}\fP.
.SS /api/status
The main fields:
.TP
.B version, uptime, stats_age
the dvbtx version, seconds since start, age of the last engine statistics.
.TP
.B engine
.BR running ,
.BR restarts ,
.B log
(its last 50 lines).
.TP
.B radios
the radios carrying multiplexes:
.BR index ,
.BR name ,
.BR driver ,
.BR center ,
.BR rate ,
.BR gain ,
.BR amp ,
and
.B live
from the engine:
.B state
.RB ( on ,
.BR off ,
.BR lost ,
.BR idle ),
.BR error ,
.BR underruns ,
.B late
(gaps reported by the radio),
.B fill
(buffer, 0 to 1),
.B cpu
(% of one core).
.TP
.B carriers
.BR index ,
.BR name ,
.BR standard ,
.BR frequency ,
.BR params ,
.BR tsid ,
.B capacity
(bit/s),
.BR radio ,
.BR enabled ,
.BR monitor ,
.B tsduck
(summary of the last report),
.B sources_load
(CPU and GPU of its channels' sources),
.B live
(engine statistics:
.BR rate ,
.BR null_rate ,
.BR si_rate ,
.BR cpu ,
per service figures) and
.BR services .
.TP
.B carriers[].services[]
.BR name ,
.BR sid ,
.BR lcn ,
.BR type ,
.BR source ,
.BR sources ,
.B active
(index of the source playing),
.B trying
(index of a preferred source being tried, or null),
.BR backup ,
.BR buffer_ms ,
.BR buffer_ms_used ,
.BR priority ,
.BR bitrate_weight ,
.BR max_bitrate ,
.BR transcoded ,
.B auto_bitrate
(target video bit rate),
.BR now ,
.BR next ,
.BR epg_events ,
.B input
(the engine's view of its source:
.BR rate ,
.BR cc_errors ,
.BR idle_ms ,
.BR slack_min_ms )
and
.B live
.RB ( rate ,
.B source
=
.BR primary | backup | none ,
.BR video_margin_min_ms ,
.BR video_margin_avg_ms ,
.BR audio_margin_min_ms ,
.BR late_max_ms ,
.BR dropped_late ,
.BR switches ).
.TP
.B inputs
the ingest processes:
.BR index ,
.BR name ,
.B kind
.RB ( ffmpeg " or " direct ),
.B role
.RB ( primary ,
.BR backup ,
.BR trial ,
.BR standby ),
.BR source ,
.BR state ,
.BR restarts ,
.BR uptime ,
.BR error ,
.BR log ,
.BR cmd ,
.B mode
(copy, audio, CPU or GPU transcode),
.B progress
(fps, speed, drop, dup),
.B usage
(cpu, gpu) and
.BR live .
.TP
.B alerts, alert_history
the active alerts
.RB ( key ,
.BR level ,
.BR message ,
.BR since )
and the last 50 alert events
.RB ( event :
.BR raise ,
.BR repeat ,
.BR clear ;
.BR time ).
.TP
.B network, thresholds, si, epg_errors, config_path, gpu, web, system, default_backup
network identity, the
.B margin_min_ms
alert threshold, SI table counters, the last EPG errors, the configuration file,
the GPU manager, whether thumbnails are shown by default, the machine load
.RB ( cpu ,
.BR cores ,
.BR gpus )
and the default backup clip.
.SS /metrics
Text format 0.0.4, every name prefixed
.BR dvbtx_ :
.TP
.B up, alerts_active
the engine runs (1/0); the number of active alerts.
.TP
.B radio_underruns_total, radio_device_gaps_total, radio_buffer_fill, radio_cpu_percent
labels
.BR radio ,
.BR driver .
.TP
.B carrier_capacity_bps, carrier_useful_bps, carrier_null_bps, carrier_si_bps, carrier_cpu_percent
labels
.BR carrier ,
.BR name .
.TP
.B service_bps, service_video_margin_min_ms, service_audio_margin_min_ms, service_late_max_ms, service_dropped_late_total, service_on_backup, service_switches_total
labels
.BR carrier ,
.BR service ,
.BR sid ,
.BR lcn .
.TP
.B input_bps, input_cc_errors_total, input_idle_ms, input_slack_min_ms, ingest_restarts_total
labels
.BR input ,
.BR name .
.SH FILES
.TP
.B /etc/dvbtx/dvbtx.toml
the configuration file the page edits
.RB ( [web]
section: listen, enabled, token, allow_exec_sources, preview_max_live,
preview_thumbnails, preview_thumb_every_s).
.TP
.IB file . name
profiles, beside the configuration file.
.TP
.IB file .bak
the file as it was before a profile was loaded.
.TP
.B /run/dvbtx/preview/thumb\-\fIsid\fP.jpg
the last thumbnail of each channel (under
.BR work_dir ).
.SH EXAMPLES
State of the transmitter, and the decoding margin of each channel:
.PP
.EX
curl \-s http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/status | jq \(aq.carriers[].services[]
    | {name, margin: .live.video_margin_min_ms}\(aq
.EE
.PP
Stop multiplex 1, then put it back on the air:
.PP
.EX
curl \-X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/carrier/1/stop
curl \-X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/carrier/1/start
.EE
.PP
Add a channel at once, with a token:
.PP
.EX
curl \-X POST \-H \(aqAuthorization: Bearer s3cret\(aq \e
     \-H \(aqContent\-Type: application/json\(aq \e
     \-d \(aq{"name": "France 24", "source": "https://example.org/live.m3u8", "lcn": 3}\(aq \e
     http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/channels
.EE
.PP
Give channel 3 two sources and a higher priority, and remove channel 0x0104:
.PP
.EX
curl \-X PATCH \-H \(aqContent\-Type: application/json\(aq \e
     \-d \(aq{"source": ["udp://239.0.0.1:2000", "/srv/videos/loop.ts"], "priority": 8}\(aq \e
     http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/channels/3
curl \-X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/channels/0x0104
.EE
.PP
Change the frequency of the first multiplex in the file, look at what is
pending, then apply:
.PP
.EX
curl \-X PATCH \-H \(aqContent\-Type: application/json\(aq \e
     \-d \(aq{"frequency": 498000000}\(aq http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/config/carrier/0
curl \-s http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/config | jq .pending
curl \-X POST http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/config/apply
.EE
.PP
Useful bit rate of DVB\-T 3/4, guard 1/8 (64\-QAM, 8k and 8 MHz by default), for 6 channels:
.PP
.EX
curl \-s \(aqhttp://127.0.0.1:8080/api/calc?standard=dvbt&code_rate=3/4&guard=1/8&services=6\(aq
.EE
.PP
Watch multiplex 0 in mpv, or open its channel 257 in VLC:
.PP
.EX
mpv http://127.0.0.1:8080/api/mux/0.ts
vlc \(aqhttp://127.0.0.1:8080/api/mux/0.m3u?program=257\(aq
.EE
.PP
Prometheus scrape job:
.PP
.EX
scrape_configs:
  \- job_name: dvbtx
    static_configs:
      \- targets: [\(aqtransmitter:8080\(aq]
.EE
